OL,3,AToxic algorithms wouldn't let them go -
OL,4,Anow Australia wants an off switch
OL,5,
OL,6,FWarning: This article contains an
OL,7,Faccount of living with an eating
OL,8,Fdisorder
OL,10,FVarsha Yajman was already
OL,11,Fself-conscious about the way she looked
OL,12,Fwhen she joined social media as a
OL,13,F13-year-old.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/18
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1792361897
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AToxic algorithms wouldn't let them go -
OL,4,Anow Australia wants an off switch
OL,5,
OL,6,FEndless workout videos making
OL,7,Fimpossible promises filled her feeds.
OL,8,FThrough the screen, girls she'd never
OL,9,Fmet urged her to sign up to dangerous
OL,10,Fcalorie challenges. Others proudly
OL,11,Fpromoted their height and weight - even
OL,12,Fthe number of times they had been sent
OL,13,Fto hospital - on their profiles in a
OL,14,Fform of twisted competition.
OL,16,FEvery night as she fell asleep, Varsha
OL,17,Fwould watch a stranger on the internet
OL,18,Fdiarising what they'd consumed that
OL,19,Fday.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/18
